## Context Signals

**Problem:** Municipal water utilities across North America lose 20-30% of treated water to leaks in aging pipe networks, costing the industry an estimated $2.6 billion annually in non-revenue water. Current detection methods rely on manual acoustic surveys that are slow, reactive, and workforce-dependent — a critical vulnerability as up to 50% of utility operators near retirement. Simultaneously, new EPA and state-level regulations are imposing compliance deadlines for water loss auditing, adding regulatory urgency to an already severe operational and financial problem.

**Solution:** AquaSense Technologies deploys networks of IoT acoustic sensors on water mains that continuously monitor pipe vibration signatures and transmit data to a cloud-based AI platform. The platform uses machine learning to detect leaks in real time, classify severity, predict pipe failure probability, and prioritize maintenance work orders by risk score. The system integrates with existing SCADA and GIS infrastructure and generates automated compliance reports for AWWA water audits, with sensors installable without excavation using low-power cellular connectivity.

**Target Customer:** Primary targets are mid-sized US municipal water utilities serving populations of 50,000–500,000 (approximately 1,200 utilities), which face significant water loss exposure but lack resources for proprietary monitoring. Secondary targets include industrial facilities with critical water infrastructure such as food and beverage manufacturers, data centers, and pharmaceutical plants.

